  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find the point of intersection of the parabola ${y}^{2}+13x-15y-2=0$ with the $x$-axis.",
  "worked_solution": "When the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0)^{2}+13x-15(0)-2 & =0 \\\\ 13x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $x$-axis at $(\\frac{2}{13},0).$",
